@prefix chg: <https://semblance.dev/ns/change#> .
@prefix mig: <https://semblance.dev/ns/migration#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix change: <https://semblance.dev/change/> .
@prefix c: <https://semblance.dev/ns/component#> .
@prefix sem: <https://semblance.dev/ns/core#> .

# What changed for whoever has to move with it: AGENTS.md, "When a component changes".

change:text-entry-disabled a chg:Change ;
    rdfs:label "A disabled text field is disabled, and no text entry takes typing while disabled"@en ;
    chg:issue <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/154> ;
    chg:motivation """c:TextArea rendered c:disabled on its native control, but c:TextField did not, and the one typing
reaction of every c:TextEntry (c:TypeText) wrote c:value and cleared c:error whatever c:disabled said, so an input
event that reached a disabled entry (from a script, or one dispatched by the host) changed it.""" ;
    chg:substance """A c:TextField with c:disabled true renders its input with the disabled attribute (as c:TextArea
already did), dimmed with a not-allowed cursor and without the hover border. c:TypeText, in SPARQL and in its
function twin (textfield:input), writes nothing for a c:TextEntry that is c:disabled: its c:value and c:error stay
as they are until c:disabled is removed. An entry without c:disabled renders and behaves as before.""" ;
    chg:forwardGuide """Nothing to move. An app that relied on writing a disabled field through input events sets
c:value directly instead.""" ;
    chg:backwardGuide """Nothing to move. Going back, a disabled c:TextField's input is editable again and typing in
any text entry writes whatever c:disabled says.""" ;
    chg:affects c:TextField , c:TextEntry .
